Demo programs for AmigaPython 2.7.18
====================================

These examples are trimmed and documented for classic AmigaOS with
Python 2.7.18.  Copy-anywhere release: run them with the Python binary
in the parent drawer (or Python:Python if you ASSIGN Python:).

  Python Demo/scripts/beer.py
  Python Demo/amiga/amiga_info.py


Drawers
-------

amiga/          Small Amiga-specific samples (amiga / os modules).

classes/        Classic class / operator overloading examples.
                (complex.py is educational; builtin complex exists.)

metaclasses/    Metaclass examples.  On 2.7 prefer new-style classes
                (subclass object) for new code; these demos still teach
                the classic metaclass hook.  Synch.py was removed (no
                thread support on this port).

scripts/        Self-contained scripts that run offline on Amiga.
                Unix-only tools (pty, regex module, mpz, lpq, ...) were
                removed.

sockets/        TCP/UDP examples.  Need bsdsocket.library (e.g. Roadshow).
                AF_UNIX, fork-based telnet, and multicast demos removed.

xml/            xml.sax / Expat samples (local files).

world/          Country code / TLD lookup (offline table).

chatserver.py   Multi-user telnet chat (needs TCP stack).


What was removed
----------------

Demos that cannot work on AmigaPython 2.7 were dropped, including:

  * import regex / regsub (gone since 2.5)
  * mpz, pty, thread, AF_UNIX, posix.fork
  * Unix-only shell tools (lpq, which, audiodev, symlink RCS trees)
  * Gopher / NNTP HTML generators aimed at Unix install paths

Upstream CPython Demo/ has many more examples; most assume Unix.


Tips
----

  * Use Amiga paths (DH0:Drawer/file), not Unix /path names.
  * Raise the Python stack for heavy demos (pi.py, large imports).
  * Start your TCP stack before sockets/ or chatserver.py.
